const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 8 Walkthrough: Pet Shop";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 8 walkthrough for the Pet Shop: the drawer with the green arrows, the cage stack, the dot panel, the tap handle, the parrot's water dispenser, the fish temperature chart and the thermostat setting 053.6 °F that drops the chest into the aquarium.";
const faqJsonLd = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What temperature do I set the thermostat to in Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 8?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "053.6 °F. The thermostat on the hexagonal aquarium only speaks Fahrenheit, and every fish on the chart is labelled in Celsius, so you have to use the conversion column printed down the left side of the chart. The 12 °C row is 53.6 °F, and the display takes four digits plus a decimal point, so you enter 0, 5, 3, 6."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Where is the fish temperature chart in the Pet Shop?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Inside the taped cardboard box on the floor of the back stockroom, against the white brick wall. Open the box and you get a folded sheet labelled as a fish chart: a Fahrenheit-to-Celsius scale down the left side and four fish with their preferred temperatures on the right. Read it with the Examine button, because the chart is the only place the game gives you the numbers."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What do I do with the tap handle?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Fit it to the sink in the back room. The sink has a spout but no handle until you put the chrome tap handle on it; once the handle is on, the tap runs and you can fill the blue water dispenser that sits in the basin. The full dispenser then clips onto the parrot cage."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I open the drawer under the counter?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The drawer front has two green oval buttons with chevrons and a small knob between them, plus a red and a green indicator light on the right. Press the chevron buttons until the drawer releases. Inside is a bowl of pet food, which goes straight into your bag."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is in the tube beside the hamster cages?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A pair of scissors. The three stacked cages each hold a hamster on a wheel, and the clear tube clipped to the side of the stack is where the scissors sit. Work the cage puzzle and the scissors end up in your inventory, which you can see from the icon that appears over the bag at the top of the screen."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I get the key and finish the Pet Shop?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Set the thermostat to 053.6 °F and a treasure chest appears in the hexagonal tank. Take the chest out of the water, open the inventory, select it and press Dismantle to get a Key. Select the Key, press Use, then tap the green door with the paw print on the left wall. The level ends on the results panel with +50 coins."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long does the Pet Shop take?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The recording finishes it in 5:38 of in-game time, which is about four minutes of actual footage once the cuts are taken out. Nothing in the level is timed and there is no fail state, so the only things that slow you down are the box in the stockroom and the Celsius-to-Fahrenheit step."}}]};
